#
# Conformance case: foundation/relcomp-subclass-relator
# AC: foundation lowering — the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) generalized
# to the PRODUCTION relator shape.
#
# Production relators are typed `a logic:Kind ; logic:subClassOf logic:Relator` — a
# class-edge to the Relator meta-class, NOT the direct `a logic:Relator` the
# relcomp-under-mediated case uses. The hasMetaClass-keyed relator markers never
# bind on that shape, so the discipline used to be wholly dormant on it. This case
# proves the generalized discipline (isRelatorClass :- subClassOfT(?C, logic:Relator))
# reaches it:
#   * ex:Devotion   — a concrete relator (a logic:Kind, subClassOf logic:Relator, no
#     logic: subclass) with ONLY ONE logic:mediates relatum (ex:Devotee) → logic:RelComp.
#   * ex:Enrollment — the same production shape with TWO DISTINCT logic:mediates relata
#     (ex:Student, ex:Course) → trips nothing (negative control).
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts (the
# Kind puns, the subClassOf edges, and the logic:mediates edges) are duplicated there
# in the named world ex:schema; these declarations are the program axioms the
# projections need.
#
# EXPECTED SIDE-ARTIFACT: logic:Relator appears here as a bare, stereotype-less
# subClassOf object (exactly as it is declared in production, `a owl:Class`), so the
# existing exactly-one-stereotype discipline fires logic:StereotypeCardinality on it.
# That is orthogonal to this case's subject; logic:Relator correctly does NOT fire
# logic:RelComp (it is not a concreteRelator — nothing makes it isRelatorClass).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/relcomp-subclass-relator/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: an under-mediated relator and a well-formed one, both in the production
# `a logic:Kind ; subClassOf logic:Relator` shape (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:Devotion   a logic:Kind ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:Devotee .
ex:Enrollment a logic:Kind ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:Student, ex:Course .
